n/Likely D; markets price Lawrence near 72%"], "rationale": "A strong Democratic midterm environment and an October Emerson poll showing Lawrence up eight offset Barrett's incumbency edge in an even district, while outside groups have heavily targeted the incumbent. Raters and prediction markets tilt Democratic but stop short of a likely outcome, keeping this in lean territory.", "watch": "Fresh polling showing a tighter race, or a late shift among independents toward Barrett, would move this back toward a pure tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District sits at even partisan lean, and first-term Republican Tom Barrett is defending the seat against Democrat William Lawrence in what has become the nation's most expensive House race, with more than $51 million spent on advertising. Outside groups have heavily targeted Barrett, while Lawrence has kept pace financially despite entering as a challenger.\n\nThe midterm environment favors Democrats, and the most recent independent poll showed Lawrence ahead by eight among likely voters, though earlier Democratic-sponsored surveys showed a much narrower race. Election forecasters are split, with several calling the race a tossup and others leaning or likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Lawrence's chances in the low seventies. The race remains competitive, with Lawrence modestly favored heading into the final week.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "